# The Windows release leg runs `scripts/release-notes.sh` through Git Bash, which chokes
# on CRLF (`$'\r': command not found`). Keep shell scripts LF wherever they're checked out.
*.sh text eol=lf

# One stray NUL byte in a source file makes git call the whole thing binary, and a binary
# file has no reviewable diff — `Designer.tsx` had exactly that (`join("\0")`) and its diffs
# were unreadable. Diff source as text regardless of what a typo puts in it.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
*.rs diff
